            <div class="prose max-w-none" x-show="lang === 'zh'">
                <p>广告账户能否长期稳定投放，不仅取决于预算和素材，也取决于资质、表述、授权与资金链路是否经得起检查。建议将合规巡检拆成“日常自查—周期复检—事件处置”三条线，并保留完整证据。</p>
<h2>1. 每周检查：账户与投放内容</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>账户状态</strong>：确认管理主页、商业账户、付款方式及授权员工是否正常；离职成员应立即移除，代理商权限应定期复核。</li>
<li><strong>资质有效期</strong>：检查营业执照、行业许可、品牌授权及代理证明，记录到期日并设置提前提醒。</li>
<li><strong>广告素材</strong>：逐条核对产品名称、价格、优惠期限、库存、性能对比和效果承诺，避免绝对化用语、虚假稀缺及无法证明的效果描述。</li>
<li><strong>落地页一致性</strong>：确保按钮、落地页与广告承诺一致，不出现强制跳转、误导下载、隐藏费用或与素材无关的内容。</li>
<li><strong>敏感品类</strong>：涉及金融、医疗、保健品、招聘、博彩或面向未成年人的产品时，应增加专项审核，不能仅凭普通行业经验判断。</li>
</ul>
<h3>素材抽检表</h3>
<p>每周按账户和广告系列抽样，记录广告 ID、投放地区、素材版本、落地页地址、审核人、问题等级及处理结果。同一模板被批量复用时，应扩大抽检范围。</p>
<h2>2. 每月检查：网站、数据与资金</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>隐私与授权</strong>：检查 Cookie 同意、隐私政策、数据处理说明及表单收集范围是否一致；埋点和广告追踪应取得有效授权。</li>
<li><strong>第三方工具</strong>：核对 CRM、像素、归因平台和数据分析工具的数据共享权限，关闭无业务用途的访问。</li>
<li><strong>充值对账</strong>：核对充值订单、平台余额、发票、支付手续费与实际扣款；差异应按账户、广告账户和时间维度定位。</li>
<li><strong>落地页技术</strong>：检查 HTTP/HTTPS、证书、跳转、移动端显示及表单提交结果，重点排查收集失败和异常跳转。</li>
<li><strong>地区规则</strong>：不同市场的消费者保护、促销披露和行业监管要求应分别建表，不宜直接套用单一模板。</li>
</ul>
<h2>3. 整改闭环：按风险分级处置</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>高风险</strong>：疑似欺诈、侵权、敏感品类违规或正在扩大的数据泄露，应立即暂停相关素材，保留截图与日志，并通知法务、安全及平台客户支持。</li>
<li><strong>中风险</strong>：资质即将到期、文案证据不足、授权不清等问题，应限期补充材料；无法证明的表述先下线，不等待活动结束。</li>
<li><strong>低风险</strong>：链接失效、提示不完整或记录缺失，可纳入常规工单修复。</li>
</ul>
<p>每项问题都应记录发现时间、责任人、截止时间、整改证据和复核结论。某工具类 App 曾因批量复用未经确认的效果表述收到平台警告；团队随后停止全部关联素材，按广告 ID 逐条复核，并补充内部证据库，避免同类问题重复发生。</p>
<h2>4. SOP 落地配置</h2>
<ul>
<li>每日自动监控账户拒审、余额异常和落地页可用性。</li>
<li>每周由投放与素材负责人完成内容抽检。</li>
<li>每月由财务、隐私或法务共同复核资质、资金和数据链路。</li>
<li>每季度更新行业规则清单，并在新国家、新产品上线前进行专项检查。</li>
<li>平台政策持续变化，最终要求应以广告平台后台规则、当地法律及企业合规意见为准。</li>
</ul>
            </div>
            <div class="prose max-w-none" x-show="lang === 'en'" x-cloak>
                <p>Long-term ad account stability depends not only on budget and creative quality, but also on verifiable credentials, compliant claims, valid permissions, and traceable funding workflows. A practical compliance program should combine daily monitoring, periodic audits, and a documented incident response process.</p>
<h2>1. Weekly checks: accounts and live ads</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Account health:</strong> Review Business Manager, ad accounts, payment methods, and user access. Remove former employees promptly and audit agency permissions on a regular basis.</li>
<li><strong>Credential validity:</strong> Check business licenses, industry permits, brand authorizations, and agency documents. Record expiry dates and set advance reminders.</li>
<li><strong>Ad creative:</strong> Verify product names, prices, promotion dates, inventory, performance comparisons, and outcome claims. Avoid absolute claims, false scarcity, or statements that cannot be substantiated.</li>
<li><strong>Landing-page consistency:</strong> Ensure that calls to action, landing pages, and ad claims align. Remove forced redirects, misleading downloads, hidden charges, and unrelated landing-page content.</li>
<li><strong>Restricted categories:</strong> Ads involving finance, healthcare, supplements, recruitment, gambling, or minors require a specialist review and documented approval.</li>
</ul>
<h3>Creative sampling sheet</h3>
<p>Sample ads weekly by account and campaign. Record the ad ID, target market, creative version, landing-page URL, reviewer, risk level, and resolution. Expand the sample whenever a template is reused across multiple campaigns.</p>
<h2>2. Monthly checks: websites, data, and funding</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Privacy and consent:</strong> Review cookie consent, privacy notices, data-processing disclosures, and form fields. Ensure tracking pixels and advertising measurement use valid permissions.</li>
<li><strong>Third-party tools:</strong> Audit access to CRM systems, pixels, attribution platforms, and analytics tools. Revoke credentials that are no longer required.</li>
<li><strong>Funding reconciliation:</strong> Compare top-up orders, platform balances, invoices, processing fees, and actual charges. Investigate discrepancies by account, ad account, and transaction date.</li>
<li><strong>Website performance:</strong> Check HTTPS, certificates, redirects, mobile rendering, and form submissions, with particular attention to failed forms and unexpected redirects.</li>
<li><strong>Market-specific rules:</strong> Maintain separate checklists for consumer protection, promotion disclosure, and industry requirements in each target market.</li>
</ul>
<h2>3. Remediation workflow: classify by risk</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>High risk:</strong> Suspected fraud, infringement, restricted-category violations, or an expanding data breach should trigger immediate pausing of affected assets, preservation of screenshots and logs, and escalation to legal, security, and platform support.</li>
<li><strong>Medium risk:</strong> Expiring credentials, insufficient evidence, or unclear permissions require deadlines and supporting documents. Remove claims that cannot be verified rather than waiting for a campaign to end.</li>
<li><strong>Low risk:</strong> Broken links, incomplete notices, and missing records can be managed through standard support tickets.</li>
</ul>
<p>Every issue should include the discovery date, owner, deadline, remediation evidence, and review result. In one example, a utility-style app reused outcome claims that had not been formally substantiated. The team paused all linked ads, reviewed them by ad ID, and built an internal evidence library to prevent recurrence.</p>
<h2>4. Operating model</h2>
<ul>
<li>Monitor account rejections, balance anomalies, and landing-page availability daily.</li>
<li>Conduct weekly creative sampling led by media and creative teams.</li>
<li>Reconcile funding and review credentials, data flows, and permissions monthly with finance, privacy, or legal stakeholders.</li>
<li>Update the market rulebook quarterly and run a targeted review before launching in a new country or product category.</li>
</ul>
<p>Platform policies change frequently. Final requirements should therefore be checked against current ad platform rules, applicable local laws, and professional compliance advice.</p>
